  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operations:\n\n- First,  we use the associative law:\n\n$$\n[(X\u2227Y)\u2228\u00acX]\u2228\u00acY\u2261(X\u2227Y)\u2228(\u00acX\u2228\u00acY)\n$$\n\n- Next,  we use a De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n(X\u2227Y)\u2228(\u00acX\u2228\u00acY)\u2261(X\u2227Y)\u2228\u00ac(X\u2227Y)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the disjunction of a statement and its negation is a tautology:\n\n$$\n(X\u2227Y)\u2228\u00ac(X\u2227Y)\u2261t\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n[(X\u2227Y)\u2228\u00acX]\u2228\u00acY\u2261t.\n$$",
